that another project was reusing drop legacy was different, but you can see the same patterns

14:35.940 --> 14:36.940
here.

14:36.940 --> 14:41.980
Like Dell will also have a secure boot chain, and yeah, we will also have some nice memory

14:41.980 --> 14:51.980
corruption vulnerability there, which I will talk about in a second.

14:51.980 --> 15:00.600
So Dell Enterprise products have a remote management function called iDRAC.

15:00.600 --> 15:05.380
It's the first thing that starts when you power on a PowerEdge server, for example.

15:05.380 --> 15:10.080
It has its own processor, its own SoC with dedicated storage with, you know, a bunch

