first slides that I showed you, you know, you could really start to think and say physical

22:38.680 --> 22:44.820
security is a lie. It's maybe one layer that you use for defense in depth, but you can't really

22:44.820 --> 22:51.880
assume that your device is protected from attacks that involve physical attacks. And if you bake

22:51.880 --> 22:55.960
this in in the design phase if you think about it when threat modeling I would

22:55.960 --> 22:59.980
really hope that some of these attacks were not possible anymore or at least

22:59.980 --> 23:05.140
very hard to pull off. This also means that users or workloads cannot be

23:05.140 --> 23:09.940
