24:57.420 --> 25:02.620
as we have seen can be quite dangerous and powerful in firmware land.

25:02.620 --> 25:09.120
But looking at the local side, even in some of the most fundamental firmware projects

25:09.120 --> 25:16.960
like edk2 you have heat buffer overflows here found by mark beethoff and actually this is a

25:16.960 --> 25:23.120
security related function this function is supposed to measure a partition table from a storage

25:23.120 --> 25:32.960
device into you know a pcr for example in a security chip and it also has a denial of service

25:32.960 --> 25:40.480
vulnerability, so nothing to see here, I guess. And then, of course, whatever I showed here also

25:40.480 --> 25:45.120
affected the local end of the attack surface with fault systems and image format parsing.

25:45.600 --> 25:51.680
Very classic parser bugs. Yeah, so I think the location of these vulnerabilities is interesting.

25:51.680 --> 25:57.840
